    for_in_unresolved_if_match_route_type_2026-10-24, 1, "2026-11-10 fable p2 lane: reproduced on the pure-Simple MIR lowering path (interpreter-run) with a TWO-module fixture, which the same-module sibling spec could not: `val route = if c: <match pick(): Ok(v): v / Err: return> else: make()` with Route/pick/make imported from lib.dep yields `for-in over non-array iterables (#143) (collection mir type: Unit)`. Root cause (mir_lowering_stmts.spl remember_merged_arm_identity -> mir_merged_arm_struct_name): the Ok-payload arm names its struct via the name-keyed bootstrap_fn_ret_ok_shape registry as BARE `Route`, the call/constructor arm names it via the consumer table's HIR return type as qualified `lib.dep::Route`; textual inequality dropped the merge slot's struct identity, so `route.items` lowered to Unit. The if-merge MirType patch from for_in_if_merge_first_arm_i64_wins does not reach this (both arms are already Struct). Fix: mir_merged_struct_name_pair unifies exactly one bare spelling with its qualified spelling (qualified kept); two differing qualified names (lib.a::Route vs lib.b::Route) still disagree. Specs: test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/for_in_if_match_cross_module_route_spec.spl (8 shapes: driver shape, match-tail, both-match, bare match, else-match, nested if, match-arm iterable, if-val) red 4/8 -> green 8/8; test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/if_merge_arm_struct_name_spec.spl (direct contract, 8/8, discriminates the two-qualified case). Neighbours unchanged: if_merge_unresolved_arm_struct_for_in_spec 1/1, if_merge_arm_types_spec 5/5, stage2_test_runner_mir_type_propagation_spec 14/14. The `val route: PackageIndexRouteV1` @workaround annotation in driver_source_pipeline_loading.spl is left in place until a stage-3 native build verifies; remove it then."

